{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1270,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vision is arguably the most compelling human\nsense. Words and stories and sounds allow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6240,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us to imagine strange beasts and faroff worlds,\nbut seeing makes us truly believe they exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12400,
    "dDurationMs": 3389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why we place so much effort into\ncorrecting the optics of our eyes when they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15789,
    "dDurationMs": 5061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't work - whether with glasses or contact\nlenses or surgery. But if you're in a pinch,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20850,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bleary-eyed or missing your glasses, there's\na simple trick that will allow you to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24620,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clearly - just make a tiny, tiny hole using\nyour fingers, look through it, and the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29380,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will become clear again. This works no matter\nhow blurry your vision is -- take off your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33900,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "glasses and give it a try!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43790,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Amazing, right?! But to explain this wizardry,\nwe just need to remember how seeing works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52149,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light travels outwards from a source, bounces\noff of objects in its path, travels into your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56219,
    "dDurationMs": 4781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eye and onto your retina, where it forms an\nimage. If your eye had no lens, light from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61000,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single source would hit your retina in lots\nof places and result in a smeared-out mess"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65100,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- which is exactly what happens when I take\nthe lens off of my camera."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68899,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lens focuses that spread-out light back\ninto a single point, corralling it into a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72149,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crisp image on your retina. And after a little\nexcitation of light-sensitive nerves and interpretation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77049,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from your brain, you see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78719,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait! When we look at an object, the background\nand foreground are usually blurry, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83509,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lens can only focus light coming from one\ndistance away. If an object is too near or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88549,
    "dDurationMs": 5441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too far, its light will again be spread out\non your retina leaving you with a blur. Fortunately,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93990,
    "dDurationMs": 4329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "muscles in our eyes allow us to accommodate\nby squeezing the lens, which changes its focal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98319,
    "dDurationMs": 4171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "length so we can see at different distances\n- except when we can't, or when our lenses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102490,
    "dDurationMs": 2629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become damaged - in which case we need glasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105119,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unlike a lens, a pinhole or other small opening\ncan focus light coming from ANY distance:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110359,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it's such a small opening, it only\nallows light to come through in one place,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114700,
    "dDurationMs": 4589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and thus in only one direction from any particular\nsource. So there's no blur, and everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119289,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is in focus!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120340,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're familiar with photography, this\nis why using smaller and smaller apertures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124049,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "makes everything in your photo come into focus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126419,
    "dDurationMs": 4961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, small openings like pinholes and\ncamera apertures create crisp images by blocking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131380,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than focusing light, so the images\nare much darker -- which is a major reason"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135890,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why we use lenses rather than pinholes for\nglasses, telescopes -- and eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140030,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, in a pinch, looking through a tiny\nhole made with your fingers can help "
    } ]
  } ]
}
